   "grounded": false,
   "answer": "imagine you're at a giant carnival. \n\nmarket makers are the guys running the game booth. when everyone buys call options (betting the stock goes up), the booth runner has to buy actual shares of the stock so they don't get wrecked if the price explodes. when everyone buys puts (betting it goes down), they sell shares. \n\n**gamma** is just how fast that booth runner has to panic-buy or panic-sell those shares when the stock starts moving. \n\nif there's a ton of gamma piled up at a certain price, it acts like a giant foam wall. the stock hits it, the booth runner is forced to buy to cover, and it bounces right back. but if it breaks through the wall? the booth runner has to chase it like a guy running for the last bus, which turns a normal move into a massive rocket ship or a straight-down elevator. \n\nstop trading 0DTEs until you know where the walls are."
  },
